{"at":"2026-10-13T12:35:55.643Z","tool":"open_session","args":"{\"issue\":11404,\"questions\":\"1. **Form of the feature.** The issue offers three alternatives (an Italic option in the panel, Ctrl+I, an italic font). Which ships? *Suggested:* an \\\"Italic\\\" toggle in the text properties next to the text align control, plus Ctrl+I (Cmd+I on macOS); no separate italic ","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:36:21.509Z","tool":"record_answers","args":"{\"issue\":11404,\"answers\":\"Answers from the product owner, relayed by the user; uncovered questions take the suggested answer.\\n\\n1. **Form of the feature (user):** An \\\"Italic\\\" toggle in the properties panel and Ctrl+I (Cmd+I on macOS); italic is one property per text element; no separate italic fo","outcome":"ok"}
{"at":"2026-10-13T12:36:57.521Z","tool":"submit_plan","args":"{\"issue\":11404,\"plan\":\"# Text properties\\nupdate C-001: start from an italic text; the text stays italic after the font family changes\\nupdate C-004: start from an italic text; add an opacity change; the text stays italic after color and opacity change\\nupdate C-006: also turn on \\\"Italic\\\" before c","outcome":"ok"}
